#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Pin what the CLI does, case by case, against recorded fixtures.

Development only; nothing in the plugin runs this. Each case in CASES builds a
home from its seeds, runs one invocation of the C CLI in it, and compares what
happened against dev/parity-cases/<name>.json, which records the behavior this
repository has agreed to keep.

Every external program the CLI can run -- the notifier, the shell, hyprctl, the
picker, OCR, ffmpeg, the agents -- is a stub that records how it was called, so
a case never touches the real desktop and the calls themselves are compared.

Compared: exit code; stdout, config.json, and the index `omoide index` hands
the shell afterwards, parsed as JSON (so spacing and key order are not
differences); the database, schema and every
row; the log; the files left in the data and state directories; and every
recorded call, including the prompt an agent was sent. stderr is not compared:
the wording of errors is allowed to change.

A behavior change is made by changing the code, re-recording the cases it
touches, and reviewing the fixture diff in the same change. A case with no
fixture fails, and so does a fixture with no case.

    dev/parity                  all cases
    dev/parity commit           cases whose name contains "commit"
    dev/parity --record commit  rewrite those fixtures from what the CLI does now
    dev/parity --cc gcc         a different compiler
    dev/parity --sanitize       the CLI under ASan and UBSan
    dev/parity --dump item      print what the CLI did, to check a case tests something
"""

